<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guadalete</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guadalete is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, flowing from the Sierra de Grazalema past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcos-de-la-frontera">Arcos de la Frontera</a> and Jerez to the Bay of Cádiz at El Puerto de Santa María. Near it in 711 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a> defeated the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roderic">Roderic</a>, opening the Muslim conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, in a battle traditionally named after the river.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guadalete.jpg" alt="Guadalete" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emilio J. Rodríguez Posada · CC BY-SA 2.5 es · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desembocadura_del_r%C3%ADo_Guadalete2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
